WEBVTT

00:02:00.557 --> 00:02:04.061
Multinational forces comprised
primarily of US Army units

00:02:04.061 --> 00:02:07.231
moved on the Belgistan capital of
Kaha, but yesterday before dawn,

00:02:07.231 --> 00:02:08.899
they were counterattacked
by Belgistan forces,

00:02:08.899 --> 00:02:11.768
and have suspended their advance.

00:02:11.768 --> 00:02:14.171
Details of this incident have
not been released,

00:02:14.171 --> 00:02:16.740
but US Army 14th Armored Calvary
Regiment Third Battalion

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:18.575
was part of the units dispatched
for this mission.

00:02:18.575 --> 00:02:20.611
This battalion has suffered devastating
losses, impacting field operations.

00:02:20.611 --> 00:02:23.380
So, you imply that the losses the
multinational forces suffered

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:27.784
actually far exceed what's been
announced by the United Nations?

00:02:27.784 --> 00:02:29.119
According to one source,

00:02:29.119 --> 00:02:34.491
Belgistan is employing a radically
new specialized weapon.

00:02:34.491 --> 00:02:36.288
A radically new specialized weapon?

00:02:41.331 --> 00:02:46.169
Yushiro and the others should be
arriving in Belgistan right about now.

00:02:46.169 --> 00:02:47.329
That's about right.

00:02:50.674 --> 00:02:54.337
Kiyotsugu and Kiyoharu will
be arriving at Narita soon.

00:02:55.646 --> 00:02:57.047
Did you inform him about
the other two?

00:02:57.047 --> 00:02:58.605
No, I did not.

00:03:00.117 --> 00:03:03.644
Well, I'm sure Takeharu will
take care of it just fine.

00:03:16.767 --> 00:03:20.137
Are you from the 3rd Experimentation
Company, SSDF Training Group?

00:03:20.137 --> 00:03:23.040
May I see Lieutenant
Colonel Hayakawa?

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:24.234
That would be me.

00:03:26.143 --> 00:03:29.813
I've been instructed to accompany you
to multinational force headquarters.

00:03:29.813 --> 00:03:32.749
I'm Lieutenant Gowa from
headquarters, Sir.

00:03:32.749 --> 00:03:33.738
Gowa?

00:03:37.454 --> 00:03:39.356
I'm his cousin.

00:03:39.356 --> 00:03:41.654
I see. Then, if you would?

00:03:47.331 --> 00:03:51.468
Another Gowa at our service,
even out here.

00:03:51.468 --> 00:03:53.904
Knock it off, Captain.

00:03:53.904 --> 00:03:57.674
International resistance to America's
hard line approach is growing

00:03:57.674 --> 00:04:02.112
following the unexpected prospects of
a long, drawn out conflict in Belgistan.

00:04:02.112 --> 00:04:04.247
EU nations are backing
the French proposal

00:04:04.247 --> 00:04:06.183
to strengthen the economic
embargo against Belgistan,

00:04:06.183 --> 00:04:09.019
while America continues
to advocate control

00:04:09.019 --> 00:04:11.121
through increased deployment
of multinational forces.

00:04:11.121 --> 00:04:15.192
It is unlikely that the multinational
forces will attack again for a while.

00:04:15.192 --> 00:04:19.526
Evacuation of the cross section
experiment facility is nearly complete.

00:04:22.933 --> 00:04:26.370
Lieutenant Gowa has informed me of
the nature of the Colonel's unit,

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.668
and I must say, I'm very interested.

00:04:29.906 --> 00:04:35.879
Due to the company's top secret
status with the multinational forces,

00:04:35.879 --> 00:04:39.116
General Dole has coordinated the
issues of your accommodation.

00:04:39.116 --> 00:04:42.219
Upon arriving in the field, we were
instructed to place ourselves

00:04:42.219 --> 00:04:45.822
within the chain of command of
the multinational forces.

00:04:45.822 --> 00:04:49.626
Will we be participating in the next
assault against the capital?

00:04:49.626 --> 00:04:53.597
No, you will be given separate orders.

00:04:53.597 --> 00:04:55.766
Explain to him, Lieutenant.

00:04:55.766 --> 00:04:57.256
Yes, Sir.

00:04:59.569 --> 00:05:00.637
Please observe carefully.

00:05:00.637 --> 00:05:01.671
This is the...

00:05:01.671 --> 00:05:05.942
Yes, the site where the weapon of
mass destruction was tested.

00:05:05.942 --> 00:05:08.912
A ruin called the Shrine Hill.

00:05:08.912 --> 00:05:12.883
Your company will conduct a raid
against this cratered area.

00:05:12.883 --> 00:05:16.253
Neutralize all resistance,
and secure the area.

00:05:16.253 --> 00:05:18.588
Wait a minute!

00:05:18.588 --> 00:05:21.258
This is deep inside enemy territory!

00:05:21.258 --> 00:05:23.460
You need not worry.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:25.228
Based on data from our spy satellites,

00:05:25.228 --> 00:05:29.399
we believe only a mechanized
platoon is stationed here.

00:05:29.399 --> 00:05:34.871
We will deploy our forces against the
capital at the time of your operation,

00:05:34.871 --> 00:05:37.396
moving ahead with new
strategic initiatives.

00:05:40.510 --> 00:05:44.848
If TA's are as good as the
Japanese claim,

00:05:44.848 --> 00:05:47.717
this operation will be a success.

00:05:47.717 --> 00:05:49.019
But...

00:05:49.019 --> 00:05:50.754
You need not worry yourself, Colonel.

00:05:50.754 --> 00:05:52.889
This operation has been authorized
by Japan's Joints Chief of Staff...

00:05:52.889 --> 00:05:56.660
I mean by the Japanese
Government itself.

00:05:56.660 --> 00:06:00.030
Official orders will arrive soon.

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:01.565
Understood.

00:06:01.565 --> 00:06:05.368
Then we should start detailing
a tactical plan.

00:06:05.368 --> 00:06:07.504
There's no need for that.

00:06:07.504 --> 00:06:11.308
We already have a detailed tactical
operations plan prepared.

00:06:11.308 --> 00:06:14.644
At 1600 hours we will
conduct a briefing,

00:06:14.644 --> 00:06:17.147
so please have your officers ready.

00:06:17.147 --> 00:06:20.917
The main force will begin
its operation tonight.

00:06:20.917 --> 00:06:26.289
The experimental company is to begin
operations tomorrow at dawn.

00:06:26.289 --> 00:06:30.894
If combat breaks out again, I wonder
where we'll be positioned?

00:06:30.894 --> 00:06:35.765
Can't say. I'd guess we'd be used as
an unassigned reserve force.

00:06:35.765 --> 00:06:38.427
You figure they don't count
on us as a major force?

00:06:39.936 --> 00:06:42.439
Yeah, I'm sure the forces already here

00:06:42.439 --> 00:06:47.277
would never consider Tactical
Armor an effective weapon.

00:06:47.277 --> 00:06:50.440
I used to think so just six months ago.

00:06:52.449 --> 00:06:56.887
But this overseas deployment is part
of TA's demonstration, right?

00:06:56.887 --> 00:07:00.457
Don't you think we might possibly end
up being assigned to the frontlines?

00:07:00.457 --> 00:07:01.691
That's true.

00:07:01.691 --> 00:07:06.096
And there's the rumor about the enemy
being equipped with TA's too.

00:07:06.096 --> 00:07:08.331
"Better to let a snake poke
around a bush,"

00:07:08.331 --> 00:07:09.499
might be what they're thinking.

00:07:09.499 --> 00:07:12.068
That might not be the case.

00:07:12.068 --> 00:07:14.638
I just heard this circulating
around here,

00:07:14.638 --> 00:07:18.141
but it seems moderates in the Security
Council are building up steam again.

00:07:18.141 --> 00:07:20.410
What?! Is that right?

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:22.071
Are you that hard up for combat?

00:07:23.079 --> 00:07:25.415
Little gets by you.

00:07:25.415 --> 00:07:29.215
The collection and analysis
of information is my job.

00:07:30.253 --> 00:07:33.523
Tomorrow morning, a special
plane is going to arrive,

00:07:33.523 --> 00:07:37.727
and it sounds like powerful moderates
are going to be on board.

00:07:37.727 --> 00:07:41.097
So, are those big shots
going to enter Kaha?

00:07:41.097 --> 00:07:45.101
The United Nations probably figured
out that letting Stilbanov save face

00:07:45.101 --> 00:07:48.071
would be the fastest
way to a cease-fire.

00:07:48.071 --> 00:07:49.739
I see.

00:07:49.739 --> 00:07:51.502
There will be combat.

00:07:52.709 --> 00:07:53.698
I'm certain.

00:07:56.947 --> 00:07:58.949
What is it, Lieutenant Murai?

00:07:58.949 --> 00:08:01.551
Orders from the Joints Chiefs of Staff.

00:08:01.551 --> 00:08:03.253
From the Joints Chiefs of Staff?

00:08:03.253 --> 00:08:06.056
Yes, and it's been assigned
a high security status.

00:08:06.056 --> 00:08:09.685
Only the Colonel can open
it with his personal code.

00:08:18.134 --> 00:08:20.604
Colonel!

00:08:20.604 --> 00:08:23.073
Have orders come in from
the Joint Chiefs of Staff?

00:08:23.073 --> 00:08:24.374
Yes, Sir.

00:08:24.374 --> 00:08:27.744
The contents have not been verified,
but we did receive it, Sir.

00:08:27.744 --> 00:08:29.879
Well, they were fast.

00:08:29.879 --> 00:08:34.084
This is a bit rushed, but we have a
briefing to attend at 1600 hours.

00:08:34.084 --> 00:08:36.820
What does this mean, Sir?

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:41.224
An investigative team is going to be
sent to the Shrine Hill explosion site.

00:08:41.224 --> 00:08:46.096
Our mission will be to remove the
enemy forces, and secure the area.

00:08:46.096 --> 00:08:49.122
The operation will start at 0300
hours tomorrow morning.

00:08:51.468 --> 00:08:53.368
These are the orders for that.

00:08:55.038 --> 00:08:57.707
Lieutenant Colonel Hayakawa, was it?

00:08:57.707 --> 00:09:01.011
He seemed to be rather surprised with
the suddenness of the mission.

00:09:01.011 --> 00:09:04.105
He's the model SSDF soldier.

00:09:07.183 --> 00:09:09.286
I can't help but notice that the
members of the Gowa family

00:09:09.286 --> 00:09:13.823
are the exception and not the norm in
what to expect from Japanese people.

00:09:13.823 --> 00:09:15.125
I will not deny that.

00:09:15.125 --> 00:09:17.460
But I'm sure one of my cousins
arriving tonight

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:20.623
will strike you as being very
typically Japanese.

00:09:24.734 --> 00:09:29.539
He is a very able administrative
secretary. I'll talk to him about you.

00:09:29.539 --> 00:09:31.941
This war will end soon.

00:09:31.941 --> 00:09:35.178
Yes, the Gowa family will
keep its promise.

00:09:35.178 --> 00:09:36.980
After returning stateside,

00:09:36.980 --> 00:09:41.076
please allow Gowa Instruments USA to
hire you as an out of office consultant.

00:09:45.221 --> 00:09:47.590
We are now coming up behind the
CB that's been sent ahead of us.

00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:49.820
All units rest in your
standby positions.

00:09:59.636 --> 00:10:02.939
I wonder why we're getting sent
out all of a sudden like this.

00:10:02.939 --> 00:10:07.010
Geez, I still haven't recovered
from jet lag.

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:10.080
If that's how you feel, then
rest while you can.

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:12.173
This will be hard on you if you don't,
Captain Kitazawa.

00:10:22.926 --> 00:10:25.462
It appears that the SB loaded
with Focus One through Four

00:10:25.462 --> 00:10:28.598
has taken to the air on schedule.

00:10:28.598 --> 00:10:33.903
But if that explosion was really the
result of a weapon of mass destruction,

00:10:33.903 --> 00:10:36.906
then we should be prepared
with specialized...

00:10:36.906 --> 00:10:39.642
I've been told we do not have to worry
about residual contamination.

00:10:39.642 --> 00:10:42.379
How can they say that?

00:10:42.379 --> 00:10:46.716
Whatever the case, the orders that
were handed down to us were official.

00:10:46.716 --> 00:10:49.378
All we can do is hope headquarters'
intelligence got it right.

00:10:52.389 --> 00:10:57.694
In a few hours, the experimental
facility will be in our hands.

00:10:57.694 --> 00:11:00.356
"Poke about a bush, and
what will come out?"

00:11:02.499 --> 00:11:06.902
What if something far more sinister
than a snake should emerge?

00:11:08.738 --> 00:11:10.433
I look forward to that.

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:26.389
CB to SB.

00:11:26.389 --> 00:11:29.692
All Focus units, switch from standby
to drop ready mode.

00:11:29.692 --> 00:11:32.829
CB to all Focus units. This
is your final briefing.

00:11:32.829 --> 00:11:35.398
We will begin countdown
2,000m west of the target.

00:11:35.398 --> 00:11:37.700
Seven seconds later, we will
enter the drop zone.

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:40.670
The drop zone is five meters
in front of the target.

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:42.872
Possibility that we will be detected in
this drop is over seventy percent.

00:11:42.872 --> 00:11:45.008
Reconfirm the path of movement.

00:11:45.008 --> 00:11:47.110
Focus One, acknowledged.

00:11:47.110 --> 00:11:48.645
Focus Two, acknowledged.

00:11:48.645 --> 00:11:50.079
Focus Three, acknowledged.

00:11:50.079 --> 00:11:51.512
Focus Four, acknowledged.

00:11:53.149 --> 00:11:55.985
While this is an operation being
conducted with little preparation,

00:11:55.985 --> 00:11:59.122
the enemy has been confirmed
to be of platoon strength.

00:11:59.122 --> 00:12:01.458
This will be your first combat mission,

00:12:01.458 --> 00:12:05.261
but I expect you will successfully
execute it as you've done in training.

00:12:05.261 --> 00:12:09.599
I tried to detect their radar once more,
but I'm not detecting any radar waves.

00:12:09.599 --> 00:12:11.901
Good. That's to our advantage.

00:12:11.901 --> 00:12:13.603
According to the latest
weather information,

00:12:13.603 --> 00:12:16.906
a low pressure front is expected
to move close to the target,

00:12:16.906 --> 00:12:21.809
but it will be noon before the
weather starts to change.

00:12:23.112 --> 00:12:25.715
5,000m and counting to target.

00:12:25.715 --> 00:12:28.183
All Focus units, prepare for impact.

00:12:30.587 --> 00:12:32.555
Platoon A, physical condition check.

00:12:32.555 --> 00:12:37.794
Heart rate, Focus One at 82,
Focus Two at 94.

00:12:37.794 --> 00:12:39.963
Platoon B, physical condition check.

00:12:39.963 --> 00:12:45.368
Heart rate, Focus Three at 85,
Focus Four at 79.

00:12:45.368 --> 00:12:46.903
Dopamine receptor readings:

00:12:46.903 --> 00:12:49.772
Focus One, Focus Two, both
report normal levels.

00:12:49.772 --> 00:12:52.707
Focus Three, Focus Four, both
report normal levels.

00:12:54.978 --> 00:12:56.546
Start countdown!

00:12:56.546 --> 00:12:57.514
6...

00:12:57.514 --> 00:12:58.515
5...

00:12:58.515 --> 00:12:59.549
4...

00:12:59.549 --> 00:13:00.550
3...

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:01.518
2...

00:13:01.518 --> 00:13:02.485
1...

00:13:02.485 --> 00:13:03.577
Drop!

00:13:46.496 --> 00:13:50.398
Focus Four, disable the enemy vehicle
together with Focus Three.

00:14:25.835 --> 00:14:30.273
So, the experimental facility has
been completely overrun?

00:14:30.273 --> 00:14:31.307
Yes, Sir.

00:14:31.307 --> 00:14:33.710
The enemy is comprised of four Fakes.

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:37.544
They appear to be those from Japan's
SSDF which arrived yesterday.

00:14:39.182 --> 00:14:43.019
There is nothing of real
value left there.

00:14:43.019 --> 00:14:44.087
What about Miharu?

00:14:44.087 --> 00:14:46.923
I've been told her condition
has finally stabilized.

00:14:46.923 --> 00:14:51.394
In any case, it'd be best to get Miharu
out of Belgistan as soon as possible.

00:14:51.394 --> 00:14:52.759
At once, Sir.

00:14:55.732 --> 00:14:57.266
Wait.

00:14:57.266 --> 00:15:01.537
If their Fakes are that well built,

00:15:01.537 --> 00:15:04.841
then one of them might be the one...

00:15:04.841 --> 00:15:09.879
The other invitator that Miharu
attempted psychological fusion with?

00:15:09.879 --> 00:15:13.082
That's not outside the
realm of possibility.

00:15:13.082 --> 00:15:16.552
Let the two have contact
with one another.

00:15:16.552 --> 00:15:17.987
But...

00:15:17.987 --> 00:15:20.751
Yes, as you wish, Sir.

00:15:58.394 --> 00:15:59.884
Why?

00:16:04.333 --> 00:16:08.137
Damn, this is no different than taking
footage of your average patrol.

00:16:08.137 --> 00:16:10.707
Couldn't get a single decent shot.

00:16:10.707 --> 00:16:12.275
Let's move out.

00:16:12.275 --> 00:16:15.578
Sounds like we'll be able to take a look
at something a lot more interesting.

00:16:15.578 --> 00:16:16.946
Something a lot more interesting?

00:16:16.946 --> 00:16:17.935
I like that!

00:16:27.423 --> 00:16:30.593
I see, so it wasn't heat.

00:16:30.593 --> 00:16:32.095
Any sign of magnetic
fluctuation signatures?

00:16:32.095 --> 00:16:33.062
We have some.

00:16:33.062 --> 00:16:35.198
Considering the amount of
time that has elapsed,

00:16:35.198 --> 00:16:37.967
I would say it must have
been more than 72.

00:16:37.967 --> 00:16:39.332
That's amazing.

00:16:42.638 --> 00:16:46.665
I did not realize Gowa representatives
would be here in person.

00:16:47.910 --> 00:16:50.980
As you can see, my older brother is a
researcher through and through.

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:54.584
I'm only helping him coordinate
the investigation.

00:16:54.584 --> 00:16:55.785
We...

00:16:55.785 --> 00:17:02.425
No, the entire world thought weapons
of mass destruction were being tested.

00:17:02.425 --> 00:17:03.960
But...

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:06.062
In fact, nothing like that took place.

00:17:06.062 --> 00:17:09.054
And you knew that before now.

00:17:10.099 --> 00:17:13.603
Just how much do you people know?

00:17:13.603 --> 00:17:16.539
And what do you intend
for us to do for you?

00:17:16.539 --> 00:17:18.871
Oh, I'm not the one who could
answer such questions.

00:17:21.511 --> 00:17:23.312
Well, this was uneventful.

00:17:23.312 --> 00:17:25.348
I guess combat can be like that.

00:17:25.348 --> 00:17:29.018
Considering the difference in strength,
you wouldn't expect another outcome.

00:17:29.018 --> 00:17:31.287
Don't let your guard down,
Captain Kitazawa.

00:17:31.287 --> 00:17:33.990
Most of this nation's defense
forces are being utilized

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:36.959
for defense of the capital and
maintaining the frontlines.

00:17:36.959 --> 00:17:40.997
In other words, there's little of
strategic value at this spot.

00:17:40.997 --> 00:17:44.567
But it'd be foolish to just assume the
enemy won't attempt a counterattack.

00:17:44.567 --> 00:17:46.728
Yes, we can't be sure.

00:17:47.770 --> 00:17:50.534
Sure wish they'd finish whatever
they're working on.

00:18:01.584 --> 00:18:03.820
I thought that participating
in this operation

00:18:03.820 --> 00:18:06.289
might let me figure out something.

00:18:06.289 --> 00:18:08.424
Where I come from.

00:18:08.424 --> 00:18:09.926
Where I'm going.

00:18:09.926 --> 00:18:11.794
Who I am.

00:18:11.794 --> 00:18:14.661
But why did I start to think like that?

00:18:31.747 --> 00:18:32.736
Captain Gowa?

00:18:48.631 --> 00:18:51.031
We are still at Defcon 3, Captain!

00:18:55.738 --> 00:18:57.406
What is it?

00:18:57.406 --> 00:18:59.809
Check the Captain's
physical condition!

00:18:59.809 --> 00:19:00.776
Yes, Sir!

00:19:09.018 --> 00:19:11.687
That's the Dance of Gasara!

00:19:11.687 --> 00:19:13.856
What are you doing, Yushiro?!

00:19:13.856 --> 00:19:15.691
Don't stop him, Kiyoharu!

00:19:15.691 --> 00:19:16.680
Brother?

00:19:17.693 --> 00:19:20.663
Think about the significance
of this place.

00:19:20.663 --> 00:19:25.401
If this space shares the same unique
attributes as the stage of stone...

00:19:25.401 --> 00:19:28.671
Observe the space around
Yushiro carefully!

00:19:28.671 --> 00:19:30.696
Don't let anything get by!

00:19:41.984 --> 00:19:44.680
Captain Gowa, what the
hell is going on?!

00:19:59.035 --> 00:20:02.305
CB-3 has captured energy readings
identical to what we had before.

00:20:02.305 --> 00:20:04.507
Confirmed GS reading as well!

00:20:04.507 --> 00:20:07.843
So the other one was in that unit.

00:20:07.843 --> 00:20:09.037
Get me Yushiro's data!

00:20:12.281 --> 00:20:15.184
His heart rate is already above 300?

00:20:15.184 --> 00:20:16.708
This might be enough for a singularity.

00:20:33.402 --> 00:20:35.029
What is that woman trying to do?

00:20:41.744 --> 00:20:43.045
Captain Gowa!

00:20:43.045 --> 00:20:43.946
Don't interrupt him!

00:20:43.946 --> 00:20:45.174
Let him keep going!

00:20:54.023 --> 00:20:55.558
Captain?

00:20:55.558 --> 00:20:57.924
Sniper, 12 o'clock!

00:21:04.433 --> 00:21:05.968
Captain! Captain Gowa!

00:21:05.968 --> 00:21:06.957
Yushiro!

00:21:20.249 --> 00:21:21.238
Coming again...

00:21:22.518 --> 00:21:23.919
Why...

00:21:23.919 --> 00:21:25.079
Why is she...

00:21:31.227 --> 00:21:32.461
Enemy attack!

00:21:32.461 --> 00:21:33.262
What?

00:21:33.262 --> 00:21:34.930
All units, prepare to intercept!

00:21:34.930 --> 00:21:36.032
Watch over the Captain!

00:21:36.032 --> 00:21:37.056
Yes, Ma'am!

00:21:45.808 --> 00:21:47.143
Captain Gowa!

00:21:47.143 --> 00:21:49.245
Confirmed enemy. Checking backup.

00:21:49.245 --> 00:21:51.280
Can't expect Focus One to help us.

00:21:51.280 --> 00:21:53.082
Three person formation, ready?

00:21:53.082 --> 00:21:54.572
Roger!

00:21:58.220 --> 00:21:59.989
Hey...

00:21:59.989 --> 00:22:00.978
What the?

00:22:04.126 --> 00:22:07.892
Those must be the TAs that the
multinational forces encountered.

00:24:00.676 --> 00:24:04.313
What makes my heart stir like this?

00:24:04.313 --> 00:24:07.750
What makes my heart hurt like this?

00:24:07.750 --> 00:24:11.287
As the glare and the smoke of
gunpowder hang in the air,

00:24:11.287 --> 00:24:13.152
sweet sad passions fly through
the battlefield.

00:24:14.423 --> 00:24:16.125
Clad in thick armor

00:24:16.125 --> 00:24:19.128
Inhibited to confirm your presence

00:24:19.128 --> 00:24:22.393
But I feel as if we touch upon
each other's wounds.

00:24:23.732 --> 00:24:27.293
Nostalgia grips my heart
in ways I never knew.
